record.field:
Temporary unemployment due to force majeure for medical reasons" means:
1° absence from work due to the suspension of the performance of the employment contract when the worker has been declared fit for work under the legislation relating to compulsory health insurance and benefits but challenges this decision before the competent authorities;
2° absence from work following the opinion of an occupational physician or a physician recognized by the unemployment office that the worker is temporarily unfit for work in the agreed position.
